{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300858-m20-enhancing-attributes-and-abilities-with-magic","id":1300858,"title":"M20 Enhancing Attributes and Abilities with magic.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-29T09:12:56-07:00","id":1300858,"title":"M20 Enhancing Attributes and Abilities with magic.","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> In M20, what Sphere and at what level is used to grant yourself more dots on an Ability or Attribute? I was thinking Life for all physical, all mental and Appareance, but not sure if mental/social are under the purview of Mind. And for Talents I was thinking Mind + Life, Skills and Knowledges just Mind.<br /> <br /> Any help appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T09:24:54-07:00","id":1300860,"title":"","content":"Mind 1 lets you improve your Mental Attributes; this includes Perception, Intelligence and Wits, and I also include Willpower in this but I don't know if that's normal.<br /> <br /> Life 2 (I believe) lets you improve your Physical Attributes, plus Appearance.<br /> <br /> How you raise Charisma and Manipulation is anyone's guess I think. I'd say Mind, or perhaps Mind/Life, but justifying it would be much easier in some Paradigms (Art of Desire for example) than others.<br /> <br /> If you raise a trait with a Sphere and get enough successes to make it Permanent, you can invest some EXP (half cost) to keep it forever. This is why Mind 1 is a great investment if you want to improve your Wits, for example.<br /> <br /> As for raising Abilities, I'm not sure. The only Mage mechanic that I know of for Ability learning is Dream/Hypercram which gives you a single Ability temporarily, and using a Grimoire, which reduces the cost of learning the Ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T11:11:25-07:00","id":1300881,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s also <i>Magick Enhancing Abilities</i> (p.533), which isn\u2019t so much about enhancing Abilities as it is about enhancing individual uses of Abilities: wield an appropriate Sphere (the example given is Entropy to enhance a Tarot card reading), roll your Arete, and apply the Arete roll\u2019s successes as difficulty reductions to the Ability roll (to a limit of -3 difficulty). You don\u2019t get more skill, talent, or knowledge; but you\u2019re more effective with what you have. <br /> <br /> That said, I <i>could</i> see gaining Ability dots using Magick. However, I\u2019d limit it to borrowing or lending Abilities: <i>someone</i> has to already have the knowledge, skill, or talent in question. Sharing (or stealing) a Knowledge would definitely be Mind; other Abilities would likely be Life, Mind, or both. <br /> <br /> And of course, both Attribute boosts and Ability boosts can be put into a Wonder or Enhancement, letting you gain the benefits on a long-term basis without the need to expend experience points \u2014 the catch being that you need to acquire enough Quintessence to make the Wonder; and if you incorporate it directly into your Pattern as an Enhancement so that you can\u2019t easily be deprived of it, you suffer some sort of downside such as a Genetic Flaw or Permanent Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T11:50:42-07:00","id":1300891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300858-m20-enhancing-attributes-and-abilities-with-magic?p=1300860#post1300860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life 2 (I believe) lets you improve your Physical Attributes, plus Appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, it's Life 4 to Increase Traits. (M20, p. 508)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T11:58:43-07:00","id":1300894,"title":"","content":"Life 4 if you want to increase Traits on others, Life 3 for yourself:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HDYDT p.21</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank 3 Life Arts (Rank 4 for other characters) can boost or lower body-based Attributes by one dot per success rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also the way it was in previous editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300858-m20-enhancing-attributes-and-abilities-with-magic?p=1300881#post1300881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I <i>could</i> see gaining Ability dots using Magick. However, I\u2019d limit it to borrowing or lending Abilities: <i>someone</i> has to already have the knowledge, skill, or talent in question. Sharing (or stealing) a Knowledge would definitely be Mind; other Abilities would likely be Life, Mind, or both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, it's true that the Ability has to come from somewhere (To create something a mage needs to know what she's doing. Thus &quot;creating&quot; knowledge would require the mage <i>to know it already</i>), but perhaps it doesn't need to come from a concrete <i>person</i>.<br /> <br /> I think a powerful mage (Mind 4, Spirit 4, perhaps Correspondence 4) could be able to directly tap into the Astral Umbra wealth of knowledge. Drinking from the rivers of knowledge, so to speak.<br /> <br /> Add Life for Skills and Talents that require training of the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T12:06:23-07:00","id":1300897,"title":"","content":"I could see Correspondence being used in this way; it is, after all, the Sphere of the Digital Web. \u201cI know Kung Fu!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T12:25:33-07:00","id":1300903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300858-m20-enhancing-attributes-and-abilities-with-magic?p=1300897#post1300897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see Correspondence being used in this way; it is, after all, the Sphere of the Digital Web. \u201cI know Kung Fu!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bit in one of the M20 books about how &quot;Download Fu&quot; isn't possible yet, but whoever cracks it will be a huge deal among the VAs (or NWO even!).<br /> <br /> I have two in-universe solutions to the problem.<br /> <br /> A principia that teaches people the Hypercram background. Poor solution but it's a good start.<br /> <br /> A network that allows a user to become possessed by a Data spirit with 5 points in the relevant ability programmed into it. An experimental version of this system with terrible bugs could be a good starting point for a story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T13:00:06-07:00","id":1300919,"title":"","content":"It's not necessarily that remarkable, though. As with Attributes, an Effect that boosts an Ability would be temporary in nature; and it would be comparable to studying a Grimoire for learning purposes. And if you wanted to make it permanent <i>without</i> spending the Experience, you could make it into a Wonder or Enhancement \u2014 but those have their own costs and flaws. A Talisman that gives you a rating in Martial Arts really isn't any more of a problem than one that boosts your Dexterity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T14:10:41-07:00","id":1300942,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the mage doesn't need to increase his abilities score, just get more dices to roll using that ability+attribute. There is a way to do that without increasing any trait?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T14:21:30-07:00","id":1300946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300858-m20-enhancing-attributes-and-abilities-with-magic?p=1300942#post1300942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the mage doesn't need to increase his abilities score, just get more dices to roll using that ability+attribute. There is a way to do that without increasing any trait?</div> </div> </div> </div>Magick in M20 can reduce difficulties, or give you more dice through raising traits. There isn't a third option that I know of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T16:12:51-07:00","id":1300974,"title":"","content":"Yeah; lowering the difficulty is the WoD way to get more successes without increasing the traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-26-2020, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T23:08:31-07:00","id":1301039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300858-m20-enhancing-attributes-and-abilities-with-magic?p=1300946#post1300946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Magick in M20 can reduce difficulties, or give you more dice through raising traits. There isn't a third option that I know of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Then the only option is raise the attribute that is related to the ability you want to use..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T02:33:16-07:00","id":1301044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300858-m20-enhancing-attributes-and-abilities-with-magic?p=1301039#post1301039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. Then the only option is raise the attribute that is related to the ability you want to use..</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I've just remembered that there is another way; the assistance/advice of spirits can grant bonus dice. So a Familiar/Totem can give a bonus, or you can awaken the spirit inside the object you're using (Spirit 3), such as a bow or a sword, and try and get bonus dice through that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T14:55:58-07:00","id":1301157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300858-m20-enhancing-attributes-and-abilities-with-magic?p=1300881#post1300881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I <i>could</i> see gaining Ability dots using Magick. However, I\u2019d limit it to borrowing or lending Abilities: <i>someone</i> has to already have the knowledge, skill, or talent in question. Sharing (or stealing) a Knowledge would definitely be Mind; other Abilities would likely be Life, Mind, or both.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see this getting actually a bit more abstract with high levels of Mind and actually Spirit. The idea is not as much to actually share/steal the knowledge of a specific person, but to actually use the power of a very concept.<br /> <br /> Let's take the mundane example of knitting. It's a very old concept. It spread from a few tribes to the whole world by now, A fundamental Skill with a capital S, that, while not everybody knows it, is an established memetic knowledge that has been spread and transferred.<br /> <br /> Instead of tapping a specific person's skills, high Mind and Spirit could allow for tapping the very Concept instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T09:27:42-07:00","id":1303971,"title":"","content":"Entropy 2 can increase Abilities for a while. &quot;Beginner's luck&quot;, you know. Not a permanent solution, but can help in extreme situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24212-mesmeroflife","name":"MesmerOfLife","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}